[[:db/retract 17592186111423 :question/answer-fields 17592186110263] {:db/id 17592186110564 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b07a943e-feb9-5e5c-823f-0048a8326fe6" "question-9f740b39-58c8-58b2-9755-cce906b6c35a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110565 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-12a69b61-bda4-5cdc-b9c6-93090eb9484f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110566 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7317b079-775e-5316-a7ce-180fb3a0e8c0" "question-4375ac91-f4dd-57cf-abab-b28e66baa865"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110567 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-237d3289-35f7-5376-a92f-b552192446e9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b07a943e-feb9-5e5c-823f-0048a8326fe6" :question/id #uuid "b07a943e-feb9-5e5c-823f-0048a8326fe6" :question/math-academy-id "q-340851" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(\\mu ,{4}^{2})$ with $P(X\\ge 3)=0.3446,$ find $\\mu .$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.6179\\,$ | $\\,0.6217\\,$ | $\\,0.6255\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.6554\\,$ | $\\,0.6591\\,$ | $\\,0.6628\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.6915\\,$ | $\\,0.6950\\,$ | $\\,0.6985\\,$ |\n\n$\\mu =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the given probability into a cumulative probability using the complement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 3) & =P(X<3) \\\\  & =1-P(X\\ge 3) \\\\  & =1-0.3446 \\\\  & =0.6554\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 3) & =0.6554 \\\\ P\\,(Z\\le \\frac{3-\\mu }{4}) & =0.6554 \\\\ Φ\\,(\\frac{3-\\mu }{4}) & =0.6554 \\\\ \\frac{3-\\mu }{4} & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.6554)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have \n\n$$\nΦ(0.40)=0.6554\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.6554)=0.40.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3-\\mu }{4} & =0.40 \\\\ 3-\\mu  & =1.60 \\\\ \\mu  & =1.40.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8d90d523-31e1-5f0f-8efe-27bdddda62ad"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8d90d523-31e1-5f0f-8efe-27bdddda62ad" :answer-field/id #uuid "8d90d523-31e1-5f0f-8efe-27bdddda62ad" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-53d6307a-364e-5b45-a243-85e1a8f8cc2d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-53d6307a-364e-5b45-a243-85e1a8f8cc2d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-53d6307a-364e-5b45-a243-85e1a8f8cc2d" :answer/id #uuid "53d6307a-364e-5b45-a243-85e1a8f8cc2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9f740b39-58c8-58b2-9755-cce906b6c35a" :question/id #uuid "9f740b39-58c8-58b2-9755-cce906b6c35a" :question/math-academy-id "q-94826" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(\\mu ,{4}^{2})$ with $P(X<2.5)=0.7881,$ find $\\mu .$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.6\\,$ | $\\,0.7257\\,$ | $\\,0.7291\\,$ | $\\,0.7324\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7580\\,$ | $\\,0.7611\\,$ | $\\,0.7642\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.7881\\,$ | $\\,0.7910\\,$ | $\\,0.7939\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the given probability into a cumulative probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<2.5)=0.7881\\,⇒\\,P(X\\le 2.5)=0.7881\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 2.5) & =0.7881 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{2.5-\\mu }{4}) & =0.7881 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{2.5-\\mu }{4}) & =0.7881 \\\\ \\frac{2.5-\\mu }{4} & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.7881)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(0.80)=0.7881\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.7881)=0.80.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2.5-\\mu }{4} & =0.80 \\\\ 2.5-\\mu  & =3.2 \\\\ \\mu  & =-0.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a58e5b87-4733-54fd-a5a6-2ec4834dc8c8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a58e5b87-4733-54fd-a5a6-2ec4834dc8c8" :answer-field/id #uuid "a58e5b87-4733-54fd-a5a6-2ec4834dc8c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3e523356-51e6-5eb9-8b16-754f02547625" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5cefab71-1972-502d-b0e9-4eeba025fe95" "answer-3e523356-51e6-5eb9-8b16-754f02547625" "answer-5894f257-4ebc-5d56-a70d-cf0e5f88980b" "answer-cf7c4b24-62e9-5b3c-92b0-6a9e6302154f" "answer-e6d35c5e-62bc-5eec-b8a3-467f34a66e46"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5cefab71-1972-502d-b0e9-4eeba025fe95" :answer/id #uuid "5cefab71-1972-502d-b0e9-4eeba025fe95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3e523356-51e6-5eb9-8b16-754f02547625" :answer/id #uuid "3e523356-51e6-5eb9-8b16-754f02547625" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5894f257-4ebc-5d56-a70d-cf0e5f88980b" :answer/id #uuid "5894f257-4ebc-5d56-a70d-cf0e5f88980b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf7c4b24-62e9-5b3c-92b0-6a9e6302154f" :answer/id #uuid "cf7c4b24-62e9-5b3c-92b0-6a9e6302154f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e6d35c5e-62bc-5eec-b8a3-467f34a66e46" :answer/id #uuid "e6d35c5e-62bc-5eec-b8a3-467f34a66e46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-12a69b61-bda4-5cdc-b9c6-93090eb9484f" :question/id #uuid "12a69b61-bda4-5cdc-b9c6-93090eb9484f" :question/math-academy-id "q-94833" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(2,{\\sigma }^{2})$ and $P(X<-1)=0.3783,$ find $\\sigma ,$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.3446\\,$ | $\\,0.3409\\,$ | $\\,0.3372\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.3821\\,$ | $\\,0.3783\\,$ | $\\,0.3745\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.4207\\,$ | $\\,0.4168\\,$ | $\\,0.4129\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the given probability into a cumulative probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<-1)=0.3783\\,⇒\\,P(X\\le -1)=0.3783\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le -1) & =0.3783 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{-1-2}{\\sigma }) & =0.3783 \\\\ Φ(-\\frac{3}{\\sigma }) & =0.3783 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.3783)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(-0.31)=0.3783\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.3783)=-0.31.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sigma } & =-0.31 \\\\ \\sigma  & ≈9.68\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto $2$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fad179a2-756e-591e-8afb-194232c3b6f4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fad179a2-756e-591e-8afb-194232c3b6f4" :answer-field/id #uuid "fad179a2-756e-591e-8afb-194232c3b6f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4e35a48b-83ad-5a61-a3f1-7f195f1064b7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e35e3297-c505-59cf-87e9-2b40589a0852" "answer-dd8135e4-0878-5169-b0ef-52cf2b36e46a" "answer-53fe27ad-e859-55d8-9328-3819e6132d39" "answer-1c4717ce-46ec-5dfd-a87b-f3dbc1bd41c7" "answer-4e35a48b-83ad-5a61-a3f1-7f195f1064b7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e35e3297-c505-59cf-87e9-2b40589a0852" :answer/id #uuid "e35e3297-c505-59cf-87e9-2b40589a0852" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7.56" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd8135e4-0878-5169-b0ef-52cf2b36e46a" :answer/id #uuid "dd8135e4-0878-5169-b0ef-52cf2b36e46a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.35" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-53fe27ad-e859-55d8-9328-3819e6132d39" :answer/id #uuid "53fe27ad-e859-55d8-9328-3819e6132d39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.56" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1c4717ce-46ec-5dfd-a87b-f3dbc1bd41c7" :answer/id #uuid "1c4717ce-46ec-5dfd-a87b-f3dbc1bd41c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9.12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e35a48b-83ad-5a61-a3f1-7f195f1064b7" :answer/id #uuid "4e35a48b-83ad-5a61-a3f1-7f195f1064b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9.68" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7317b079-775e-5316-a7ce-180fb3a0e8c0" :question/id #uuid "7317b079-775e-5316-a7ce-180fb3a0e8c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-341988" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(0,{\\sigma }^{2})$ is a normal random variable with $P(-1.5<X<1.5)=0.3472,$ use the table to find $\\sigma ,$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.6331\\,$ | $\\,0.6368\\,$ | $\\,0.6406\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.6700\\,$ | $\\,0.6736\\,$ | $\\,0.6772\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.7054\\,$ | $\\,0.7088\\,$ | $\\,0.7123\\,$ |\n\n$\\sigma ≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the cumulative probability using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1.5<X<1.5) & =0.3472 \\\\ 2P(0<X<1.5) & =0.3472 \\\\ P(0<X<1.5) & =0.1736 \\\\ P(X<1.5)-P(X<0) & =0.1736 \\\\ P(X<1.5)-0.5 & =0.1736 \\\\ P(X<1.5) & =0.6736 \\\\ P(X\\le 1.5) & =0.6736\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 1.5) & =0.6736 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{1.5-0}{\\sigma }) & =0.6736 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{1.5}{\\sigma }) & =0.6736 \\\\ \\frac{1.5}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.6736)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(0.45)=0.6736\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.6736)=0.45.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1.5}{\\sigma } & =0.45 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{1.5}{0.45} \\\\ \\sigma  & ≈3.33\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-69166d64-5e97-5c32-8220-3b2a1f609032"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-69166d64-5e97-5c32-8220-3b2a1f609032" :answer-field/id #uuid "69166d64-5e97-5c32-8220-3b2a1f609032" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-5d6f0a73-e2e0-5875-93f7-c3a9c8822865" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5d6f0a73-e2e0-5875-93f7-c3a9c8822865"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5d6f0a73-e2e0-5875-93f7-c3a9c8822865" :answer/id #uuid "5d6f0a73-e2e0-5875-93f7-c3a9c8822865" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.33" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4375ac91-f4dd-57cf-abab-b28e66baa865" :question/id #uuid "4375ac91-f4dd-57cf-abab-b28e66baa865" :question/math-academy-id "q-342034" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(0,{\\sigma }^{2})$ is a normal random variable with $P(|X|<3)=0.5468,$ find ${\\sigma }^{2}.$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7704\\,$ | $\\,0.7734\\,$ | $\\,0.7764\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.7995\\,$ | $\\,0.8023\\,$ | $\\,0.8051\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.8264\\,$ | $\\,0.8289\\,$ | $\\,0.8315\\,$ |\n\n${\\sigma }^{2}≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express the given probability as\n\n$$\nP(|X|<3)=P(-3<X<3).\n$$\n\nThen, we find the cumulative probability using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-3<X<3) & =0.5468 \\\\ 2P(0<X<3) & =0.5468 \\\\ P(0<X<3) & =0.2734 \\\\ P(X<3)-P(X<0) & =0.2734 \\\\ P(X<3)-0.5 & =0.2734 \\\\ P(X<3) & =0.7734 \\\\ P(X\\le 3) & =0.7734\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 3) & =0.7734 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{3-0}{\\sigma }) & =0.7734 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{3}{\\sigma }) & =0.7734 \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.7734)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(0.75)=0.7734\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.7734)=0.75.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sigma } & =0.75 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{3}{0.75} \\\\ \\sigma  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =(4)^{2}=16.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0824e9dc-c8d0-5712-a1a3-cb7ecbf153de"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0824e9dc-c8d0-5712-a1a3-cb7ecbf153de" :answer-field/id #uuid "0824e9dc-c8d0-5712-a1a3-cb7ecbf153de" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-9cdaf6c6-dec3-5b38-a91c-2be375299096" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9cdaf6c6-dec3-5b38-a91c-2be375299096"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9cdaf6c6-dec3-5b38-a91c-2be375299096" :answer/id #uuid "9cdaf6c6-dec3-5b38-a91c-2be375299096" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186111423 :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(\\mu ,{3}^{2})$ is a normal random variable with $P(-0.7\\mu <X<2.7\\mu )=0.3256,$ find $\\mu $ rounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.6217\\,$ | $\\,0.6255\\,$ | $\\,0.6293\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.6591\\,$ | $\\,0.6628\\,$ | $\\,0.6664\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.6950\\,$ | $\\,0.6985\\,$ | $\\,0.7019\\,$ |\n\n*Hint: Note that the interval $-0.7\\mu <X<2.7\\mu $ is symmetric about the mean $\\mu .$*" :question/worked-solution "Note that we can write the given probability as\n\n$$\nP(\\mu -1.7\\mu <X<\\mu +1.7\\mu )=0.3256,\n$$\n\nwhich tells us that the interval $-0.7\\mu <X<2.7\\mu $ is symmetric about the mean $\\mu .$\n\nFirst, we find the cumulative probability using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\mu -1.7\\mu <X<\\mu +1.7\\mu ) & =0.3256 \\\\ 2P(\\mu <X<\\mu +1.7\\mu ) & =0.3256 \\\\ P(\\mu <X<\\mu +1.7\\mu ) & =0.1628 \\\\ P(X<\\mu +1.7\\mu )-P(X<\\mu ) & =0.1628 \\\\ P(X<\\mu +1.7\\mu )-0.5 & =0.1628 \\\\ P(X<\\mu +1.7\\mu ) & =0.6628 \\\\ P(X\\le \\mu +1.7\\mu ) & =0.6628 \\\\ P(X\\le 2.7\\mu ) & =0.6628\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 2.7\\mu ) & =0.6628 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{2.7\\mu -\\mu }{3}) & =0.6628 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{1.7\\mu }{3}) & =0.6628 \\\\ \\frac{1.7\\mu }{3} & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.6628)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(0.42)=0.6628\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.6628)=0.42.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1.7\\mu }{3} & =0.42 \\\\ 1.7\\mu  & =1.26 \\\\ \\mu  & ≈0.741\\,18 \\\\ \\mu  & ≈0.74.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1b3114c1-4daa-5e9a-8186-cd37d952aa3f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1b3114c1-4daa-5e9a-8186-cd37d952aa3f" :answer-field/id #uuid "1b3114c1-4daa-5e9a-8186-cd37d952aa3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fa154a6e-7b02-5897-b84b-0b4cfd53f21b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c77996be-b841-5a9e-9afd-b3001a00c48c" "answer-fa154a6e-7b02-5897-b84b-0b4cfd53f21b" "answer-2c678ed7-d187-5b4d-b65e-df460c846e37" "answer-0900ee31-7fc8-5a71-bfb0-567ce40867a6" "answer-929c9f87-8068-54c6-a062-0aad2ba05db7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c77996be-b841-5a9e-9afd-b3001a00c48c" :answer/id #uuid "c77996be-b841-5a9e-9afd-b3001a00c48c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.52" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa154a6e-7b02-5897-b84b-0b4cfd53f21b" :answer/id #uuid "fa154a6e-7b02-5897-b84b-0b4cfd53f21b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.74" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c678ed7-d187-5b4d-b65e-df460c846e37" :answer/id #uuid "2c678ed7-d187-5b4d-b65e-df460c846e37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0900ee31-7fc8-5a71-bfb0-567ce40867a6" :answer/id #uuid "0900ee31-7fc8-5a71-bfb0-567ce40867a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-929c9f87-8068-54c6-a062-0aad2ba05db7" :answer/id #uuid "929c9f87-8068-54c6-a062-0aad2ba05db7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-237d3289-35f7-5376-a92f-b552192446e9" :question/id #uuid "237d3289-35f7-5376-a92f-b552192446e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-94890" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(\\mu ,{5}^{2})$ is a normal random variable with $P(-0.8\\mu <X<2.8\\mu )=0.7458,$ find $\\mu ,$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.8485\\,$ | $\\,0.8508\\,$ | $\\,0.8531\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.1\\,$ | $\\,0.8708\\,$ | $\\,0.8729\\,$ | $\\,0.8749\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.2\\,$ | $\\,0.8907\\,$ | $\\,0.8925\\,$ | $\\,0.8944\\,$ |\n\n*Hint: Note that the interval $-0.8\\mu <X<2.8\\mu $ is symmetric about the mean $\\mu .$*" :question/worked-solution "Note that we can write the given probability as\n\n$$\nP(\\mu -1.8\\mu <X<\\mu +1.8\\mu )=0.7458,\n$$\n\nwhich tells us that the interval $-0.8\\mu <X<2.8\\mu $ is symmetric about the mean $\\mu .$\n\nFirst, we find the cumulative probability using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\mu -1.8\\mu <X<\\mu +1.8\\mu ) & =0.7458 \\\\ 2P(\\mu <X<\\mu +1.8\\mu ) & =0.7458 \\\\ P(\\mu <X<2.8\\mu ) & =0.3729 \\\\ P(X<2.8\\mu )-P(X<\\mu ) & =0.3729 \\\\ P(X<2.8\\mu )-0.5 & =0.3729 \\\\ P(X<2.8\\mu ) & =0.8729 \\\\ P(X\\le 2.8\\mu ) & =0.8729\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 2.8\\mu ) & =0.8729 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{2.8\\mu -\\mu }{5}) & =0.8729 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{1.8\\mu }{5}) & =0.8729 \\\\ \\frac{1.8\\mu }{5} & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.8729)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(1.14)=0.8729\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.8729)=1.14.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1.8\\mu }{5} & =1.14 \\\\ 1.8\\mu  & =5.7 \\\\ \\mu  & ≈3.166\\,67 \\\\ \\mu  & ≈3.17.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e61ff356-8ad3-5164-a0c6-b21e9a847a8e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e61ff356-8ad3-5164-a0c6-b21e9a847a8e" :answer-field/id #uuid "e61ff356-8ad3-5164-a0c6-b21e9a847a8e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-37635532-f28a-53e6-ae9d-3b79e5b093b8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d88c6cd0-f17d-5079-9478-4d437c156ca5" "answer-6d43d3be-0f5b-5f12-af73-e68463fd21f6" "answer-29c5beaa-2bd5-5a17-8ed7-0f68efb5d37f" "answer-37635532-f28a-53e6-ae9d-3b79e5b093b8" "answer-f6c68472-5317-5646-8c48-47295237b963"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d88c6cd0-f17d-5079-9478-4d437c156ca5" :answer/id #uuid "d88c6cd0-f17d-5079-9478-4d437c156ca5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d43d3be-0f5b-5f12-af73-e68463fd21f6" :answer/id #uuid "6d43d3be-0f5b-5f12-af73-e68463fd21f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.52" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-29c5beaa-2bd5-5a17-8ed7-0f68efb5d37f" :answer/id #uuid "29c5beaa-2bd5-5a17-8ed7-0f68efb5d37f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.91" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-37635532-f28a-53e6-ae9d-3b79e5b093b8" :answer/id #uuid "37635532-f28a-53e6-ae9d-3b79e5b093b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.17" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f6c68472-5317-5646-8c48-47295237b963" :answer/id #uuid "f6c68472-5317-5646-8c48-47295237b963" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.52" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186111917 :tutorial/content "It's often helpful to use the symmetry properties of the normal distribution to help us determine unknown parameters.\n\nFor example, suppose we have the following normal random variable with unknown variance $\\sigma^2{:}$\n\n$$\nX \\sim N(1, \\sigma^2)\n$$\n\nSuppose we also know that\n\n$$\nP(-2 \\lt X \\lt  4) = 0.8714.\n$$\n\nThe interval $-2 \\lt X \\lt  4$ and the area associated with the probability that $X$ lies within this interval are shown below.\n\n![](images/11/1101c2617de9f63394c7aa7da89fd7590ab401d792ba38e0c9c5fa8f8c4e9330.png)\n\nThe endpoints of the interval $(-2,4)$ both lie at a distance of ${\\color{red}{3}}$ from the mean $\\mu.$ So, this interval is symmetric about the mean, and we can write the given probability as follows:\n\n$$\nP(\\mu - {\\color{red}{3}} \\lt X \\lt  \\mu + {\\color{red}{3}}) = 0.8714\n$$\n\nBy symmetry, the total shaded equals twice the area between the mean $\\mu$ and the right endpoint:\n\n$$\n2P(\\mu < X < \\mu + 3) = 0.8714\n$$\n\nDividing this equation by $2,$ we get\n\n$$\nP(\\mu < X < \\mu + 3) = 0.4357.\n$$\n\nLet's write this probability in terms of $Z\\sim N(0,1)$ by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\frac{\\mu -\\mu }{\\sigma }<\\frac{X-\\mu }{\\sigma }<\\frac{\\mu +3-\\mu }{\\sigma })=0.4357\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis simplifies to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0<Z<\\frac{3}{\\sigma })=0.4357.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting this in terms of $\\Phi,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\Phi\\left(\\dfrac{3}{\\sigma}\\right)  - \\Phi(0) = 0.4357\n$$\n\nand since we know that $\\Phi(0) = 0.5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\Phi\\left(\\dfrac{3}{\\sigma}\\right)  - 0.5= 0.4357\n$$\n\nwhich we can write as\n\n$$\n\\Phi\\left(\\dfrac{3}{\\sigma}\\right) = 0.9357\\qquad\\Rightarrow\\qquad \\dfrac{3}{\\sigma} = \\Phi^{-1}(0.9357).\n$$\n\nLet's now take a look at the table of values for $\\Phi(z),$\n\n| $z$ | $\\, 0.00 \\,$ | $\\, 0.01 \\,$ | $\\, 0.02 \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\, 1.4 \\,$ | $\\, 0.9192 \\,$ | $\\, 0.9207 \\,$ | $\\, 0.9222 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 1.5 \\,$ | $\\, 0.9332 \\,$ | $\\, 0.9345 \\,$ | $\\, 0.9357 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 1.6 \\,$ | $\\, 0.9452 \\,$ | $\\, 0.9463 \\,$ | $\\, 0.9474 \\,$ |\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\Phi(1.52) = 0.9357 \\quad \\Longrightarrow \\quad \\Phi^{-1}(0.9357) = 1.52.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve for $\\sigma{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sigma } & =1.52 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{3}{1.52} \\\\ \\sigma  & ≈1.974\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110839 :activity/expected-seconds 1500.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
